<title>USA: FSA lists secondary market insurance capacity.</title>
<headline>FSA lists secondary market insurance capacity.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Monday it has secondary market insurance capacity for the following issuers:</p>
<p>--California State Public Works Board lease revenue bonds issued for the Department of Corrections.</p>
<p>--New York City general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Commonwealth of Puerto Rico GOs.</p>
<p>--Puerto Rico Public Building Authority.</p>
<p>--Puerto Rico Highway Authority.</p>
<p>Insurance is available on maturities 2004 and longer and there is no par limit per firm, FSA said.</p>
<p>For more information, call 212-826-0601.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
